/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.1 Principles of Quadrants and Orthographic Projections) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Orthographic projection is a parallel projection technique where projection rays are) Tj
T*
(perpendicular to the projection plane:) Tj
T*
(* Principal Planes of Projection: Horizontal Plane \(HP\) and Vertical Plane \(VP\). The) Tj
T*
(intersection line of HP and VP is called the Reference Axis or Ground Line \(XY line\).) Tj
T*
(* Four Spatial Quadrants:) Tj
T*
(- 1st Quadrant: Above HP, In front of VP \(Observer -> Object -> Plane\). Standard in) Tj
T*
(Indian / European engineering.) Tj
T*
(- 2nd Quadrant: Above HP, Behind VP \(HP and VP overlap when rotated 90 deg clockwise;) Tj
T*
(both views fall above XY\).) Tj
T*
(- 3rd Quadrant: Below HP, Behind VP \(Observer -> Plane -> Object\). Standard in American) Tj
T*
(/ Canadian engineering.) Tj
T*
(- 4th Quadrant: Below HP, In front of VP \(Both views fall below XY line when HP is) Tj
T*
(rotated 90 deg clockwise\).) Tj
T*
(* Standard Notation Rules:) Tj
T*
(- Point in space: Capital letter \(e.g., A, B, P\).) Tj
T*
(- Elevation / Front View \(on VP\): Lowercase with prime \(e.g., a'', b'', p''\).) Tj
T*
(- Plan / Top View \(on HP\): Lowercase without prime \(e.g., a, b, p\).) Tj
T*
(- Side / End View \(on Profile Plane PP\): Lowercase with double prime \(e.g., a'''',) Tj
T*
(b''''\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.2 Projection of Points in Different Quadrants) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Case 1: Point in 1st Quadrant \(d1 above HP, d2 in front of VP\): a'' is d1 above XY;) Tj
T*
(a is d2 below XY.) Tj
T*
(* Case 2: Point in 2nd Quadrant \(d1 above HP, d2 behind VP\): Both a'' \(d1\) and a \(d2\)) Tj
T*
(are above XY.) Tj
T*
(* Case 3: Point in 3rd Quadrant \(d1 below HP, d2 behind VP\): a is d2 above XY; a'' is) Tj
T*
(d1 below XY.) Tj
T*
(* Case 4: Point in 4th Quadrant \(d1 below HP, d2 in front of VP\): Both a'' \(d1\) and a) Tj
T*
