/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.3 Projection of Straight Lines: Geometric Orientations) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A straight line is the shortest locus between two points in 3D space:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Line Parallel to both HP and VP: Both front and top views show True Length \(TL\)) Tj
T*
(and are parallel to XY.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Line Perpendicular to HP: Top view is a point; Front view is a vertical line) Tj
T*
(perpendicular to XY showing True Length.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Line Perpendicular to VP: Front view is a point; Top view is a vertical line) Tj
T*
(perpendicular to XY showing True Length.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Line Inclined to HP and Parallel to VP: Front view shows True Length and true) Tj
T*
(inclination angle theta. Top view is shorter than TL \(apparent length\) and parallel) Tj
T*
(to XY.) Tj
T*
(* 5. Line Inclined to VP and Parallel to HP: Top view shows True Length and true) Tj
T*
(inclination angle phi. Front view is apparent length and parallel to XY.) Tj
T*
(* 6. Line Inclined to both HP and VP \(Oblique Line\): Neither view shows True Length;) Tj
T*
(both views are apparent lengths \(Elevation Length EL and Plan Length PL\) inclined at) Tj
T*
(apparent angles alpha and beta.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.4 True Length and Traces of a Line) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Traces of a Straight Line:) Tj
T*
(- Horizontal Trace \(HT\): The point of intersection of the line \(or line produced\) with) Tj
T*
(the Horizontal Plane. Since HT lies on HP, its front view h'' lies on the XY line.) Tj
T*
(- Vertical Trace \(VT\): The point of intersection of the line \(or line produced\) with the) Tj
T*
(Vertical Plane. Since VT lies on VP, its top view v lies on the XY line.) Tj
T*
(* Methods to Determine True Length and Inclinations from Projections:) Tj
T*
(- 1. Rotating Line Method: Rotate elevation or plan view until parallel to XY line, then) Tj
T*
(project to find True Length.) Tj
T*
(- 2. Trapezoid Method: Construct right-angled trapezoid using difference in distances of) Tj
T*
(endpoints from reference plane.) Tj
T*
(- 3. Auxiliary Plane Method: Set up an auxiliary plane parallel to the apparent view.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
