T*
(- Draw XY line. Mark a'' 15 mm above XY and a 20 mm below XY on the same vertical) Tj
T*
(projector.) Tj
T*
(* Step 2: Locus Lines of End B:) Tj
T*
(- Assume line parallel to VP, inclined at theta = 30 deg to HP: Draw a''b1'' = 75 mm at) Tj
T*
(30 deg to horizontal. Height of b1'' gives vertical locus of B: h_B = 15 + 75 x sin\(30\)) Tj
T*
(= 15 + 37.5 = 52.5 mm above XY.) Tj
T*
(- Assume line parallel to HP, inclined at phi = 45 deg to VP: Draw ab2 = 75 mm at 45 deg) Tj
T*
(to horizontal. Distance of b2 gives horizontal locus of B: d_B = 20 + 75 x sin\(45\) = 20) Tj
T*
(+ 53.03 = 73.03 mm below XY.) Tj
